rst and circuit depth then increasing; finite deterministic angles depend on the desired accuracy and are independent of system size and disorder. No quantitative finite-size estimate, depth bound, or efficient angle-selection procedure is claimed. The whole manuscript argument has not been independently reviewed here and has no retained Lean circuit-convergence target.","citation_ids":["qaoa_main_theorem","qaoa_routes","scope_281"],"evidence_ids":["source_bytes_verified","qaoa_manuscript_review_not_run","manuscript_alignment_not_run"],"id":"qaoa_thermodynamic_first","kind":"goal","label":"QAOA approaches the SK optimum in the thermodynamic-first limit","locator":"Theorem thm:main, lines 111–119","source_id":"qaoa_introduction","statement":"For the Gaussian zero-field SK model, lim_{p→∞} Q_p = P_star, where Q_p is the supremum over deterministic p-layer angles of the limiting expected energy per spin as n→∞. Equivalently, for each epsilon>0, some finite p and deterministic angles, independent of n and the disorder, attain at least P_star-epsilon in that limiting expectation.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/qaoa_thermodynamic_first","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/qaoa_thermodynamic_first","id":"field:b44d8309619108dd85d83b8f6e56e449ea83790e26595c8d63089255c9556ce0","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/qaoa_thermodynamic_first","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/assumptions.qaoa_model_and_limits"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","id":"sha256:f22708f318006894